  "question": {
    "text": "In the circle given below, let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> unit, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn></math> unit and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>&#8869;</mo><mi>O</mi><mi>B</mi></math>. Then, the area of the triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>B</mi></math> (in square units) is :<p><img src=\"assets\\qt0097_5defcc39223c.png\" style=\"width: 315px; height: 230px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>26</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>26</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Since x-axis is normal to the circle at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math>, and normal to the circle passes through its centre. So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;is a diameter.</p><p>Now, perpendicular from centre of circle to chord bisects the chord, so&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Also, product of segments of chords in a circle is equal i.e.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>Q</mi></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>&nbsp;units</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0097_6d485fd3ea59.png\" style=\"width: 314px; height: 230px;\" /></p><p>Now, area of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math></p><p>i.e.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>12</mn></math>&nbsp;sq. units</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>&nbsp;sq. units</p>"
  }
}